source: tests/help.rs
expression: text
---
A zoxide-like fuzzy directory jumper

Usage: furet <COMMAND>

Commands:
  add      Record a visit to a directory
  query    Rank recorded directories and print the best match, falling back to a disk walk (SPEC section 11) when nothing matches
  up       Print the ancestor `n` levels above the current directory
  back     Print the second-to-last directory visited in this session
  history  Print the visit history, newest first, as tab-separated lines
  init     Print shell integration code for the requested shell
  queries  Inspect the query journal (SPEC section 15)
  list     List known directories as tab-separated lines
  stats    Print database statistics as tab-separated lines
  remove   Forget known directories matching a name or path pattern
  alias    Manage named directory aliases
  mark     Manage numbered marks (aliases named 1-9)
  home     Print the configured home directory, or nothing when unset or invalid
  import   Import directories recorded by another tool, read from stdin
  export   Print the whole database as versioned JSON, for backup or another machine
  preview  List a directory's contents for the fzf preview pane
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

PowerShell functions (defined by `furet init pwsh`):
  f <query>        Jump to the best match; -l scopes to the git project,
                   -h to the home
  f                Jump to the home directory
  f -   f -N       Go back 1 or N directories in this session
  f ..  f ...      Go up one level per extra dot (.. = 1, ... = 2)
  f !name          Jump to an alias, or a mark with f !3
  fi [query]       Pick interactively (fzf, else a numbered menu);
                   fi ! lists aliases and marks
  fm               List marks; fm 3 sets, fm -d 3 / fm -d! delete,
                   fm + / fm - cycle
  fh [-a] [-n N]   Show the visit history, numbered like f -N; -a lists every
                   session unnumbered, -n N caps the lines
  fq [-n N]        Show the query journal, newest first; --failures lists
                   the probable mistakes
`f` is renamed with `--cmd <name>`; `fi`, `fm`, `fh` and `fq` keep their names.
Ctrl+Alt+Right / Ctrl+Alt+Left run fm + / fm - on an empty line.

Database file: <DATA_DIR>\furet.db
Config file: <DATA_DIR>\config.toml (not found, defaults apply)
Log directory: <DATA_DIR>\logs
Build date: <BUILD_DATE>
